@* CheckboxGroup's Overview, written by hand after MultiSelect's, which binds the same way:
   several choices (and what an empty one posts), descriptions, select all, at least one, and
   states.
   Accessibility and See also come from the doc comment. *@

<Heading Level="2">Usage</Heading>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Usage</Code>
<TextBlock>A checkbox group is a list of checkboxes, one for each option, from which the user checks any number. It suits short lists where every option should be in view. For a long list, see <Anchor Href="docs/components/multi-select">MultiSelect</Anchor>, which needs less room. For one yes-or-no choice, see <Anchor Href="docs/components/checkbox">Checkbox</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Several choices</Heading>
<TextBlock>The group's value is the collection of checked options. Set <Code>@@bind-Value</Code> to a collection and pass the options to <Code>Items</Code>. Each checked box posts its value, so the group works <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">with JavaScript off</Anchor>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="checkbox-group-toppings" />
<List>
    <ListItem>The collection can be an array, a <Code>List&lt;T&gt;</Code>, a <Code>HashSet&lt;T&gt;</Code>, or an interface they implement.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>For an enum, pass its values to <Code>Items</Code>: <Code>Enum.GetValues&lt;Topping&gt;()</Code>.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>With no box checked, the group posts nothing. On static pages the property is then null, or the model isn't bound at all. So set defaults only when the request isn't this form's post, as this example does (<Anchor Href="docs/troubleshooting/empty-selection">why</Anchor>).</ListItem>
</List>

<Heading Level="2">Descriptions</Heading>
<TextBlock>A description is a line of text under an option's name. Screen readers hear it after the name, as the box's description. Set <Code>ItemDescription</Code> to add one to each option. For markup in the name itself, such as a badge beside it, set <Code>ItemTemplate</Code>; all of it names the box.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="checkbox-group-descriptions" />

<Heading Level="2">Select all</Heading>
<TextBlock>A select-all box sits above the options and checks or clears them all at once. Set <Code>SelectAll</Code> to add it. To change its text ("Select all" by default), set <Code>SelectAllText</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="checkbox-group-everything" />
<List>
    <ListItem>The select-all box doesn't post; the options do, as before.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>On static pages, <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">IzzyBlazor's script</Anchor> runs the box. With JavaScript off it isn't shown, and the user checks each option.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>On interactive pages, <Code>ValueChanged</Code> runs once for each option the box changes. Code that saves on every change sees each step.</ListItem>
</List>

<Heading Level="2">At least one</Heading>
<TextBlock>A group can require the user to check at least one box. Add <Code>[Required]</Code> and <Code>[MinLength(1)]</Code> together to the property.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="checkbox-group-at-least-one" />
<TextBlock>The browser can't require one of several boxes, so the validator checks it:</TextBlock>
<List>
    <ListItem>On static pages, it checks when the form posts. An empty choice leaves the property null, and <Code>[Required]</Code> catches it.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>On interactive pages, it checks on Save and as the last box is cleared. An empty choice is an empty list, and <Code>[MinLength(1)]</Code> catches it.</ListItem>
</List>
<TextBlock>Screen readers don't hear the asterisk. They hear "(required)" after the label instead (<Code>IzzyText.Required</Code>). After a form post that fails, the group's first box receives focus, so its error is read.</TextBlock>
<TextBlock>A form post can contain values that aren't among the options, and they reach the model. This example checks them on the server. Before trusting a posted value, see <Anchor Href="docs/common/forms#values-a-form-post-can-change">Values a form post can change</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Sizes and disabled</Heading>
<TextBlock>The size lines the group up with buttons and other fields. Set <Code>Size</Code> to choose one. For choices that can't change, set <Code>Disabled</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="checkbox-group-states" />
<TextBlock>There's no <Code>ReadOnly</Code>, because HTML has no read-only checkbox. In a read-only <Anchor Href="docs/components/form">Form</Anchor>, the group is disabled while a hidden field posts its value. A disabled group posts nothing. Before saving a disabled value from a form post, see <Anchor Href="docs/common/forms#disabled-fields-and-form-posts">Disabled fields and form posts</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Labels and localization</Heading>
<TextBlock>The select-all box has its own text. To set it for the whole app, see <Anchor Href="docs/common/text">Text and other languages</Anchor>.</TextBlock>
<Prose Class="site-table ib-scroll">
    <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Sets</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><Code>SelectAllText</Code></td><td>The select-all box's text</td><td>"Select all"</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</Prose>

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<OverviewSeeAlso Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string Usage = """
        @* An enum's values. *@
        <CheckboxGroup @bind-Value="Model!.Toppings" Items="Enum.GetValues<Topping>()" />

        @* Strings, in a row. *@
        <CheckboxGroup @bind-Value="Model!.Sizes" Items="AllSizes" Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" />
        """;
}
